# Snyk policy file. Suppressions are deliberate and justified; do not add one
# without a reason a reviewer can evaluate.
version: v1.25.0

ignore:
  SNYK-CC-AWS-426:
    - "*":
        reason: >-
          EC2 API termination protection is deliberately not enabled on the
          Timesketch appliance. The appliance is stateless by design: all
          persistent state (OpenSearch indices, PostgreSQL) lives on the EBS
          data volume owned by the platform layer, which carries
          prevent_destroy = true. Accidental termination therefore costs a
          re-apply, not evidence.

          Enabling it would actively break two documented workflows. The
          appliance uses user_data_replace_on_change = true, so a template
          change replaces the instance; and instance_type is specified as a
          per-incident dial that responders raise for a large case and drop
          back afterwards. Snyk's own guidance notes this rule "may prevent
          IaC workflows from updating the instance".

          Revisit if the appliance ever holds state of its own.
        expires: 2027-09-14T00:00:00.000Z
        created: 2026-09-14T00:00:00.000Z
